PART 6: THE KEY PROP - CRITICAL FOR PERFORMANCE

================================================================================

What is the key Prop?

The
key
prop is:

• A unique identifier for each item • Helps React track which items changed • Essential for list performance • Prevents bugs with state and animations • Required when rendering lists

Why Keys Matter:

// Without key - React doesn't know which item changed
{books.map(book => (
  <li>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ No key
))}

// With key - React knows exactly which item changed
{books.map(book => (
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ✓ Has key
))}
================================================================================

Good vs Bad Keys

Good Key: Unique ID

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ✓ Best
))}
Acceptable Key: Index (for static lists)

{books.map((book, index) => (
  <li key={index}>{book.title}</li>  // ⚠️ Only if list doesn't change
))}
Bad Key: No Key

{books.map(book => (
  <li>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ Causes bugs
))}
Bad Key: Random Value

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={Math.random()}>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ Changes every render
))}
================================================================================

When Index as Key Causes Problems

// Problem: If list items are reordered, index changes
const [items, setItems] = useState(['Apple', 'Banana', 'Orange'])

// User removes 'Banana'
// Now 'Orange' is at index 2 instead of 3
// React thinks 'Orange' is still at index 3
// Causes bugs!

{items.map((item, index) => (
  <li key={index}>{item}</li>  // ❌ Index changes when list reorders
))}
================================================================================

PART 7: BEST PRACTICES

================================================================================

Best Practice 1: Always Use Unique Keys

Good:

{books.map(book => (
  <Book key={book.id} book={book} />
))}
Avoid:

{books.map(book => (
  <Book book={book} />  // ❌ No key
))}
Why: • React needs to track items • Prevents bugs • Better performance

================================================================================

Best Practice 2: Use ID from Data

Good:

const books = [
  { id: 1, title: 'Book 1' },
  { id: 2, title: 'Book 2' }
]

{books.map(book => (
  <Book key={book.id} book={book} />
))}
Avoid:

{books.map((book, index) => (
  <Book key={index} book={book} />  // ❌ Index as key
))}
Why: • ID is stable • Index changes when list reorders • ID is more reliable

================================================================================

Best Practice 3: Keep map() Simple

Good:

{books.map(book => (
  <Book key={book.id} book={book} />
))}
Avoid:

{books.map(book => (
  <div key={book.id}>
    <h2>{book.title}</h2>
    <p>{book.author}</p>
    <p>{book.price}</p>
    {/* Complex logic */}
  </div>
))}
Why: • Easier to read • Easier to maintain • Use components instead

================================================================================

Best Practice 4: Extract to Component

Good:

{books.map(book => (
  <BookCard key={book.id} book={book} />
))}
Avoid:

{books.map(book => (
  <div key={book.id} className="book-card">
    {/* All book display logic here */}
  </div>
))}
Why: • Reusable component • Easier to test • Better organization

