PART 8: COMMON MISTAKES

================================================================================

Mistake 1: Missing Key Prop

Wrong:

{books.map(book => (
  <li>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ No key
))}
Warning:

Warning: Each child in a list should have a unique "key" prop
Correct:

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ✓ Has key
))}
================================================================================

Mistake 2: Using Index as Key for Dynamic Lists

Wrong:

{books.map((book, index) => (
  <li key={index}>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ Index changes when list reorders
))}
Correct:

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ✓ Stable ID
))}
================================================================================

Mistake 3: Using Random Values as Key

Wrong:

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={Math.random()}>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ Changes every render
))}
Correct:

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ✓ Stable ID
))}
================================================================================

Mistake 4: Forgetting Parentheses in Arrow Function

Wrong:

{books.map(book => 
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ❌ Works but inconsistent
)}
Correct:

{books.map(book => (
  <li key={book.id}>{book.title}</li>  // ✓ Clear and consistent
))}
================================================================================

Mistake 5: Complex Logic Inside map()

Wrong:

{books.map(book => (
  <div key={book.id}>
    {book.title}
    {book.price > 10 ? (
      <p>Expensive</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Affordable</p>
    )}
    {book.rating > 4 ? (
      <p>Highly Rated</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Good</p>
    )}
  </div>
))}
Correct:

{books.map(book => (
  <BookCard key={book.id} book={book} />
))}
Why: • Easier to read • Easier to maintain • Better organization

